es above zero one is 20 degrees  below zero  so big picture for any given number  there's a negative version of it for  example this right over here would be  positive six  and then you could have negative six  but negative 6 is 6 below 0 or 6 left of  the 0 on the number line while positive  6 is of course 6 above 0.  so i will leave you there you might be  thinking oh wow this looks a lot like a  subtraction sign maybe it is related to  subtraction somehow or how can i do  addition and subtraction multiplication  and division with negative numbers and  for that we will go to future videos
 

